} pub fn estimate_remote_cost( caps: &ConnectorCapabilities, stats: &TableStats, workload: &QueryWorkload,
) -> CostEstimate Cost factors: Selectivity — estimated fraction of rows matching filters (default: 0.1 for equality, 0.33 for range) Network — estimated_rows × avg_row_bytes (reduced by projection and filter pushdown) Latency class — Low (1x), Medium (3x), High (10x) multiplier on network cost Concurrency — max_concurrent_queries limits parallel fan-out The planner uses costs to decide: Join order — smaller (cheaper) side becomes the build side Build vs probe — build the hash table from the side with fewer estimated rows Pushdown depth — push more operations to high-latency connectors to reduce network cost

